-- protocol
ok   GET /health 200
ok   TE+CL -> 400, hidden request is not executed
ok   chunked body is decoded
ok   valid trailer is accepted
ok   space before chunk size -> 400
ok   invalid trailer -> 400
ok   Content-Length in trailer -> 400
ok   total trailer size is limited
ok   tab in request line -> 400
ok   duplicate Content-Length -> 400
ok   Content-Length 5abc -> 400
ok   TE in HTTP/1.0 -> 400 and response stays HTTP/1.0
ok   HTTP/1.1 without Host -> 400
ok   empty Host in HTTP/1.1 -> 400
ok   absolute-form: Host ignored per RFC 9112
ok   header terminator split across three reads is found
ok   16 pipelined requests in one packet -> 16 responses
ok   pipelined good + malformed: 200 is sent before 400
ok   pipelined response is sent before 100 Continue
ok   pipelined good + stuck handler: 200 then 504 from reaper
ok   handler sees client disconnect via client_gone?
ok   client_gone? is false while the client waits
ok   client_gone? follows platform semantics with unread bytes pending
ok   ClientGone closes the connection without a 500 response
ok   GET * -> 400
ok   invalid status: 500 with full body; next response remains aligned
ok   OPTIONS * -> 204 with method list
ok   authority-form without CONNECT -> 400
ok   CONNECT -> 501
ok   chunked with oversized extensions -> 400 (overhead limit)
ok   multiple Set-Cookie headers reach the client
ok   large response is received in full
ok   HEAD for large response: length present, no body
ok   TE gzip (chunked is not last) -> 400
ok   TE gzip, chunked (unknown coding) -> 501
ok   duplicate chunked coding -> 400
ok   unknown Expect -> 417
ok   more than 100 headers -> 431
ok   response includes Date
ok   413 reaches a client still sending its body
ok   Host with space -> 400
ok   IPv6 Host with port is accepted
ok   Host with invalid percent escape -> 400
ok   absolute-form is routed and replaces Host
ok   userinfo in absolute-form -> 400
ok   absolute-form scheme is case-insensitive
ok   method is case-sensitive -> 405
ok   body > max_body -> 413
ok   HEAD: same Content-Length as GET, no body
ok   204 does not corrupt next keep-alive response
ok   100 Continue without Content-Length, then 200
ok   //admin is distinct from /admin
ok   %20 is decoded in route parameter
ok   %00 in path -> 400
ok   unsupported method -> 405 with Allow
ok   header containing CR/LF is discarded
-- strict chunked boundaries
ok   invalid extension "3;" -> 400
ok   invalid extension "3;=x" -> 400
ok   invalid extension "3;foo=\"" -> 400
ok   invalid extension "3;foo=bad space" -> 400
ok   invalid extension "3;foo=" -> 400
ok   valid size/extension "3;foo=\"a\\\"b\""
ok   valid size/extension "3 ; foo = bar"
ok   valid size/extension "0000000000000003"
ok   very large hex size -> 413 without overflow
ok   absolute-form without Host -> 400
ok   origin-form without Host -> 400
-- deadlines
ok   ctx.sleep hits deadline -> fast 504
ok   handler that ignores deadline is killed by reaper -> 504
ok   pool wait is bounded by deadline -> 504
ok   resource held during with is closed after kill; slot restored
ok   next checkout lazily creates a new resource
ok   CpuPool: 504; task after deadline was not started
ok   CpuPool remains alive
ok   five stuck requests at once -> all receive 504
-- write timeout
ok   write reaches response body
ok   expired write deadline closes the connection
-- in-flight request accounting
ok   200 requests served on one connection
ok   in-flight request set is empty (no leak)
-- lifecycle: slot held until thread exits
ok   slot stays occupied after kill while thread is alive
ok   client received 504 from reaper
ok   slot restored after thread exits
ok   shutdown during cleanup releases slot and connection
-- shutdown
ok   in-flight is 0; reaper killed exactly eight threads
ok   shutdown returned 0
ok   idle keep-alive connection closed without kill
ok   repeated shutdown is safe
